Finding: {"title":"No verification that the authenticated user owns/belongs to the flightSchoolId or studentId supplied in the request body/query","severity":"CRITICAL","area":"Multi-tenant isolation / IDOR","files":["src/server/routes/routes-micamp.ts"],"detail":"Every route in this file resolves `flightSchoolId` and `studentId` directly from the client-supplied request body or query string (e.g. POST /micamp/cards L281-288, GET /micamp/cards L358-359, POST /micamp/payments L441-448, GET /micamp/payments L561-562, POST /micamp/connect L88-95, PUT /micamp/config L248, POST /micamp/disconnect L219). `requireAuth()`/`requireAdmin()` (src/server/middleware/auth.ts L153-306) only checks that a valid session exists and that its role matches an allowed list — it never binds the session's own school/tenant or student identity to the IDs used in the query. `authUser` is used only to *stamp* audit fields (`processedByUserId`, `connectedByUserId` — routes-micamp.ts L133,147,164,473,538,635,650,710,725), never as an authorization check against the resource being acted on. Any authenticated user (a student, or an admin of School A) can pass another school's `flightSchoolId` or another student's `studentId` and read/charge/tokenize/refund against it.","impact":"A student session can view another student's stored card metadata (GET /micamp/cards), view another student's/school's payment history (GET /micamp/payments), or — via POST /micamp/payments with useStoredCard=true — trigger a charge against another student's stored card token by supplying their studentId + flightSchoolId, since the only ownership check is 'does a card row exist matching these params' (L491-497), not 'does this card belong to the caller'. An admin session for one flight school can call requireAdmin()-gated routes (connect/disconnect/config/void/refund) against a different school's flightSchoolId with no tenant check, since requireAdmin() only checks role, not org membership. This directly violates ADR-002 (multi-tenant isolation) and is a live production issue on a billing-locked surface (real payment processor, real money).","recommendation":"Every route must derive the caller's own flightSchoolId (and, for student-scoped routes, verify the caller IS that studentId or an admin of that student's school) from the authenticated session — the same resolveOrgIdFromSession()/managedSchoolId pattern already used elsewhere in the codebase (referenced but never applied here) — and reject/403 when the request body's flightSchoolId/studentId doesn't match. This is a billing-locked file requiring a BILLING-APPROVED token per CLAUDE.md before modification.","confidence":"high"}
